The function is already minimal, so the gain here is small at best. The rewrite reads `profile` and `profileIndex` once into locals. It also marks the "no profile" path as unlikely, so the compiler lays out the common path straight through. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 0;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(idx >= p->numFields, 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numSubFields;
}
```